{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"agent_message","text":"I’ll use a 2×2 study: feedback in the selector versus item-only selection, crossed with joint gradients versus allowing only click gradients into the shared selector trunk. All four task losses and the model’s capacity stay fixed.\n\nThis adapts a known gradient-routing idea; STEM already separates forward sharing from backward updates. The question here is narrower: whether that separation helps history selection in this benchmark. The current results do not establish gradient conflict. [STEM paper](https://arxiv.org/html/2308.13537v2)"}}
